{"version":2,"text":"5\n\nIn the fifth paragraph, what point is made about COHb levels?\n\nA They fail to detect CO poisoning in habitual smokers.\n\nB They are a generally reliable indicator of CO poisoning.\n\n6\n\n7\n\n8\n\nC\n\nThey correlate very well with extreme levels of CO poisoning.\n\nD\n\nThey are most useful in determining intermediate levels of CO poisoning.\n\nThe phrase 'one such factor'​ in the sixth paragraph refers to\n\nA\n\na type of care.\n\nB\n\na cause of difficulty.\n\nC\n\na method of detection.\n\nD\n\na way of making an assessment.\n\nOne result of administering oxygen to CO poisoned patients in transit is that\n\nA\n\nit becomes harder to ascertain when the COHb level peaked.\n\nB\n\nit may lead to changes in the type of symptoms observed.\n\nC\n\nit could artificially inflate the COHb level in the short term.\n\nD\n\nit affects the ability to assess the effects at tissue level.\n\nWhat reservation about the CO-Oximeter does the writer express?\n\nA\n\nIt does not always give an immediate result.\n\nB\n\nIts use needs to be approved by a physician.\n\nC\n\nIt requires a skilled analyst to interpret the readings.\n\nD\n\nIt does not show variations in the patient's condition.\n\nPage 205","layout":{"version":1,"width":596.0,"height":843.0,"blocks":[{"text":"5","lines":[{"text":"5","x":0.12090684563758389,"y":0.15017181257413997,"width":0.01026566107382551,"height":0.018575293001186228,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"5","x":0.12090684563758389,"width":0.01026566107382551,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"In the fifth paragraph, what point is made about COHb levels?","lines":[{"text":"In the fifth paragraph, what point is made about COHb levels?","x":0.15365264597315437,"y":0.1503023487544484,"width":0.5048254379194631,"height":0.01776596915776986,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"In","x":0.15365264597315437,"width":0.015393583892617453,"confidence":1},{"text":"the","x":0.17417414932885908,"width":0.025659884228187914,"confidence":1},{"text":"fi